@page "/privacy"
@page "/terms"
@page "/help"
@inject NavigationManager Nav
<PageTitle>@Title · VeganAdda</PageTitle>
<article class="narrow prose"><a class="back-link" href="/"><Icon Name="arrow_back" />Back to the Adda</a><span class="eyebrow">A community built on trust</span><h1>@Title</h1>
@if (Kind is "privacy" or "terms") { <div class="feedback error"><Icon Name="pending" /><span>Draft for owner review before launch. These terms and privacy details require legal review and completed operator/contact details.</span></div> }
@if (Kind == "privacy") { <h2>Your profile, your choice</h2><p>Only profiles that opt into public visibility appear to visitors. Your name, photo, city, bio, interests, non-dating intentions and optional links are shared on your profile. Do not add private contact information to these fields.</p><p>Signed-in members can discover nonpublic profiles. Dating intention is visible only when both members opt in. Event attendees appear only to signed-in members when they separately choose attendee visibility.</p><h2>Accounts and conversations</h2><p>Google is used for sign-in. VeganAdda stores the Google account subject identifier and display name, not Google access tokens or email addresses. Essential session and security cookies keep you signed in and protect form submissions.</p><p>Messages are stored on the server and are accessible only to their conversation participants. They are not end-to-end encrypted. Removing or blocking a connection stops further messages but retains existing history for both participants.</p><h2>Deletion and safety</h2><p>Account deletion removes your profile, relationships, saves, attendance, media and entire conversations involving your account. Abuse reports are retained without the deleted account identity. Backups may retain deleted data until the backup retention period expires.</p><p>Owner review required: operator identity, grievance contact, retention schedule, backup expiry, processor details, lawful grounds, user data requests and applicable Indian privacy requirements.</p> }
else if (Kind == "terms") { <h2>Adults only, people first</h2><p>You must be 18 or older and provide accurate personal profile information. Accounts are for individuals. Do not impersonate others, harass, discriminate, spam, solicit deceptively, or share private information without consent.</p><h2>Connect with consent</h2><p>Chat requires an accepted connection. Respect a declined request, a block, and another person's boundaries. Dating is an optional private intention, not permission to send unwanted approaches.</p><h2>Gatherings</h2><p>Events are curated by the community team. Attendance on VeganAdda is not an official registration, ticket, organizer endorsement or guarantee. Confirm practical details with the organizer and use any official registration link separately.</p><h2>Moderation and service</h2><p>Members can block and report. Administrators may review reports and suspend accounts. Owner review required: moderation appeals, operator identity, contact channel, liability, governing law and dispute resolution.</p> }
else { <h2>Pull up a chair. Be kind.</h2><p>VeganAdda is a place for friendship, ideas, shared interests, dating by mutual opt-in, and activism. Treat people with dignity. Ask before giving advice, respect a no, and give every conversation room to grow.</p><h2>Your comfort comes first</h2><p>Open a member's profile to report or block them. Blocking hides your profiles from each other and closes messaging. You can manage blocked members in your settings. Never share another person's personal details without their consent.</p><h2>Feedback & event suggestions</h2><p>Owner action required before launch: add a monitored community support and grievance contact here. No feedback submission channel is configured yet.</p><p>To report a specific member, use the report form on their profile. Event suggestions will need organizer details, verified times, venue, and an official information link.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/settings">Your privacy settings<Icon Name="arrow_forward" /></a> }
</article>
@code { string Kind => Nav.ToBaseRelativePath(Nav.Uri).Split('?')[0]; string Title => Kind == "privacy" ? "Privacy, with care." : Kind == "terms" ? "Our terms of belonging." : "The community agreement."; }

